A||N||6||FieroJoe||Gorlic 4cyl exhaust a good buy?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||05-23-2001||10:43 AM||||Yes, I have read up on this.  Found some good topics from a while back.  It seems to me that everyone who has purchased the Fiero Store's Gorlic stock exhaust system has been pleased.<P>Mine is pretty bad.  The muffler has a few holes, and the pipe is about non-existent.  The exhaust system might very well be over 50,000 miles old or more (the car has 220,000).<P>The kit is for sale right now at $90, chromed twin tips included (which I need).  Is this a good buy?  I dont really want to go with a flowmaster, I bet it'd sound pretty crappy on a 4cyl.  I do plan on removing my cat and replacing it with either a straight pipe or cherry bomb, so that would be the extent of my exhaust mods.  The rest of the system just needs to be replaced.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-23-2001||08:30 PM||||bump!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||05-23-2001||10:30 PM||||The Gorlic exhaust is a stock exhaust, you<BR>could go for the Ocelot perfromance system<BR>instead. I don't know how the 4cyl Ocelot is<BR>but I put the V6 version on my GT and it sounds pretty good. <BR>I would suggest painting the exhaust with a high temp paint to keep it from rusting.<BR>Also; if you're going to be driving the car in bad weather you might want to change to<BR>stainless tips,the chrome ones will rust fast<BR>if they are used in wet or snowy weather.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||05-23-2001||10:43 PM||||Hey Joe!<BR>Your exhaust system is rusting out???<BR>I have an 84 2M4 with 250K miles including Michigan salt winters...<BR>That exhaust is still original stainless and hole less...<BR>Did someone replace it with steel pipes?!?<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||05-24-2001||04:05 PM||||I'll have to look into that ocelot system...price wise that is.<P>Fierowrecker - Yes, it must have been replaced at one time or another.  The car has never been driven winters though.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||05-25-2001||12:04 AM||||Would you like to have an original system?<BR>My parts car has a complete exhaust system intact...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
